i scalar"],["line","reference","the threshold, $p = 1$"]],"caption":["The Kretschmann scalar $K$ and the Ricci scalar $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ of a massless scalar field falling in from infinity and dispersing, against $x$ ($p = 9/10$), the same at every $\\theta$ and $\\phi$, beside the threshold $p = 1$. Each line of constant $\\tau$ is a light ray moving out, $u = -2\\ell e^{-\\tau}$, and $K\\,\\ell^4e^{-4\\tau} = Ku^4/16$ depends on $x$ alone, so on every ray $K$ is $16/u^4$ times a function of $x$ alone. On every light ray moving out, $u = -2\\ell e^{-\\tau}$, $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ is $4/u^2$ times a function of $x$ alone, since $R^\\mu{}_\\mu\\,\\ell^2e^{-2\\tau} = R^\\mu{}_\\mu u^2/4$ depends on $x$ alone. Along every line of constant $x$, $K$ grows as $u^{-4}$ toward $u = v = 0$, where the field's first ray reaches the centre.","On the first ray, $x = 0$, $K$ vanishes, as in the flat space before it. It stays below the threshold's at every $x$ and is greatest at $x = 0.318$, where $K\\,\\ell^4e^{-4\\tau} = 0.113$. Far out it falls as $R^{-6}$ in the areal radius $R$, as Schwarzschild's does. $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ vanishes on the first ray and is negative at every $x > 0$, above the threshold's, and least at $x = 0.318$, where $R^\\mu{}_\\mu\\,\\ell^2e^{-2\\tau} = -0.194$. Far out it falls off as $R^{-3}$ in the areal radius $R$. At every event the Kretschmann scalar is three times the square of the Ricci scalar."],"ricci_sentences":[[0,2],[1,3],[1,4]],"per_scalar":{"kretschmann":{"opening":"The Kretschmann scalar $K$ of a massless scalar field falling in from infinity and dispersing, against $x$ ($p = 9/10$), the same at every $\\theta$ and $\\phi$, beside the threshold $p = 1$.","clip":"We draw $K\\,\\ell^4e^{-4\\tau}$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-6}$ to $10^{4}$, the same in every view, and cut each curve where it leaves its panel: each $K$ passes below $10^{-6}$ within $x = 0.0004$ of the first ray, where it vanishes, and at $p = 9/10$ beyond $x = 2.14$.","legend":[["line","K","$K$, the Kretschmann scalar"],["line","reference","the threshold, $p = 1$"]]},"ricci_scalar":{"opening":"The Ricci scalar $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ of a massless scalar field falling in from infinity and dispersing, against $x$ ($p = 9/10$), the same at every $\\theta$ and $\\phi$, beside the threshold $p = 1$.","clip":"We draw $R^\\mu{}_\\mu\\,\\ell^2e^{-2\\tau}$ on a signed logarithmic scale, linear within $10^{-6}$ of zero, from $-10^{2}$ to $0$, the same in every view, and every value drawn lies within it.","legend":[["line","R","$R^\\mu{}_\\mu$, the Ricci scalar"],["line","reference","the threshold, $p = 1$"]]}},"settings":"$p = 9/10$ and $\\tau = 0$, the light ray $u = -2\\ell$, with $\\ell$ any length, the unit of every length.","clip":"We draw $K\\,\\ell^4e^{-4\\tau}$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-6}$ to $10^{4}$ and $R^\\mu{}_\\mu\\,\\ell^2e^{-2\\tau}$ on a signed logarithmic scale, linear within $10^{-6}$ of zero, from $-10^{2}$ to $0$, the same in every view, and cut each curve where it leaves its panel: each $K$ passes below $10^{-6}$ within $x = 0.0004$ of the first ray, where it vanishes, and at $p = 9/10$ beyond $x = 2.14$; every $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ drawn lies within its scale."},{"id":"threshold","label":"$p = 1$","kind":"line","x":{"name":"$x$","from":0,"to":3,"ticks":[{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"},{"at":0.5,"label":"$0.5$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$1$"},{"at":1.5,"label":"$1.5$"},{"at":2.0,"label":"$2$"},{"at":2.5,"label":"$2.5$"},{"at":3.0,"label":"$3$"}]},"panels":[{"id":"K","name":"$K\\,\\ell^4e^{-4\\tau}$","aspect":2,"scale":{"kind":"log","from":1e-06,"to":10000.0},"ticks":[{"at":1e-06,"label":"$10^{-6}$"},{"at":0.0001,"label":"$10^{-4}$"},{"at":0.01,"label":"$10^{-2}$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$10^{0}$"},{"at":100.0,"label":"$10^{2}$"},{"at":10000.0,"label":"$10^{4}$"}]},{"id":"R","name":"$R^\\mu{}_\\mu\\,\\ell^2e^{-2\\tau}$","aspect":2,"scale":{"kind":"symlog","from":-100.0,"to":0,"linear":1e-06},"ticks":[{"at":-100.0,"label":"$-10^{2}$"},{"at":-1.0,"label":"