ainst $x$ ($p = 1$), the same at every $\\theta$ and $\\phi$. Each line of constant $\\tau$ is a light ray moving out, $u = -2\\ell e^{-\\tau}$, and $K\\,\\ell^4e^{-4\\tau} = Ku^4/16$ depends on $x$ alone, so on every ray $K$ is $16/u^4$ times a function of $x$ alone. On every light ray moving out, $u = -2\\ell e^{-\\tau}$, $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ is $4/u^2$ times a function of $x$ alone, since $R^\\mu{}_\\mu\\,\\ell^2e^{-2\\tau} = R^\\mu{}_\\mu u^2/4$ depends on $x$ alone. Along every line of constant $x$, $K$ grows as $u^{-4}$ toward $u = v = 0$, where the field's first ray reaches the centre.","Here $K\\,\\ell^4e^{-4\\tau} = 3(1 - e^{-2x})^2e^{-4x}$, which vanishes on the first ray, $x = 0$, is greatest, $3/16$, at $x = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\ln 2 = 0.347$, and far out falls as $R^{-4}$ in the areal radius $R$, more slowly than Schwarzschild's $R^{-6}$. Here $R^\\mu{}_\\mu\\,\\ell^2e^{-2\\tau} = -(1 - e^{-2x})e^{-2x}$, least, $-1/4$, at $x = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\ln 2$, and far out it falls off as $R^{-2}$ in the areal radius $R$. The null singularity $u = 0$, where the spheres shrink to zero area, lies at $\\tau = \\infty$, and toward it $K$ grows as $12/u^2v^2$ on every ray of constant $v$. Toward the null singularity $u = 0$, $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ falls without bound as $2/uv$ on every ray of constant $v$. At every event the Kretschmann scalar is three times the square of the Ricci scalar."],"ricci_sentences":[[0,2],[1,1],[1,3]],"per_scalar":{"kretschmann":{"opening":"The Kretschmann scalar $K$ of a massless scalar field falling in from infinity on the threshold of making a black hole, against $x$ ($p = 1$), the same at every $\\theta$ and $\\phi$.","clip":"We draw $K\\,\\ell^4e^{-4\\tau}$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-6}$ to $10^{4}$, the same in every view, and cut each curve where it leaves its panel, as $K$ does within $x = 0.0003$ of the first ray, where it vanishes.","legend":[["line","K","$K$, the Kretschmann scalar"]]},"ricci_scalar":{"opening":"The Ricci scalar $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ of a massless scalar field falling in from infinity on the threshold of making a black hole, against $x$ ($p = 1$), the same at every $\\theta$ and $\\phi$.","clip":"We draw $R^\\mu{}_\\mu\\,\\ell^2e^{-2\\tau}$ on a signed logarithmic scale, linear within $10^{-6}$ of zero, from $-10^{2}$ to $0$, the same in every view, and every value drawn lies within it.","legend":[["line","R","$R^\\mu{}_\\mu$, the Ricci scalar"]]}},"settings":"$p = 1$ and $\\tau = 0$, the light ray $u = -2\\ell$, with $\\ell$ any length, the unit of every length.","clip":"We draw $K\\,\\ell^4e^{-4\\tau}$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-6}$ to $10^{4}$ and $R^\\mu{}_\\mu\\,\\ell^2e^{-2\\tau}$ on a signed logarithmic scale, linear within $10^{-6}$ of zero, from $-10^{2}$ to $0$, the same in every view, and cut each curve where it leaves its panel, as $K$ does within $x = 0.0003$ of the first ray, where it vanishes; $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ lies within its scale."},{"id":"collapses","label":"$p = 2$","kind":"line","x":{"name":"$x$","from":0,"to":0.6,"ticks":[{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"},{"at":0.1,"label":"$0.1$"},{"at":0.2,"label":"$0.2$"},{"at":0.3,"label":"$0.3$"},{"at":0.4,"label":"$0.4$"},{"at":0.5,"label":"$0.5$"},{"at":0.6,"label":"$0.6$"}]},"panels":[{"id":"K","name":"$K\\,\\ell^4e^{-4\\tau}$","aspect":2,"scale":{"kind":"log","from":1e-06,"to":10000.0},"ticks":[{"at":1e-06,"label":"$10^{-6}$"},{"at":0.0001,"label":"$10^{-4}$"},{"at":0.01,"label":"$10^{-2}$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$10^{0}$"},{"at":100.0,"label":"$10^{2}$"},{"at":10000.0,"label":"$10^{4}$"}]},{"id":"R","name":"$R^\\mu{}_\\mu\\,\\ell^2e^{-2\\tau}$","aspect":2,"scale":{"kind":"symlog","from":-100.0,"to":0,"linear":1e-06},"ticks":[{"at":-100.0,"label":"$-10^{2}$"},{"at":-1.0,"label":"$-10^{0}$"},{"at":-0.01,"label":"$-10^{-2}$"},{"at":-0.0001,"label":"$-10^{-4}$"},{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"}]}],"curves":[{"panel":"K","class":"reference","metric":"roberts","system":"scaling","scalar":"kretschmann","coordinate":"x","fixed":{"\\tau":0.0},"params":