$ alone. On every light ray moving out, $u = -2\\ell e^{-\\tau}$, $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ is $4/u^2$ times a function of $x$ alone, since $R^\\mu{}_\\mu\\,\\ell^2e^{-2\\tau} = R^\\mu{}_\\mu u^2/4$ depends on $x$ alone. Along every line of constant $x$, $K$ grows as $u^{-4}$ toward $u = v = 0$, where the field's first ray reaches the centre.","Every light ray moving out ends on the singularity $x_s = \\tanh^{-1}(1/p) = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\ln 3 = 0.549$, where the spheres shrink to zero area. $K$ stands above the threshold's at every $x$ and grows toward the singularity as $1/108(x_s - x)^4$. Past the apparent horizon, $x = \\tanh^{-1}(1/p^2) = 0.255$, where $K\\,\\ell^4e^{-4\\tau} = 27/4$, the spheres along each ray shrink. $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ is negative at every $x > 0$, below the threshold's, and falls without bound toward the singularity $x_s = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\ln 3$ as $-1/18(x_s - x)^2$. At every event the Kretschmann scalar is three times the square of the Ricci scalar."],"ricci_sentences":[[0,2],[1,3]],"per_scalar":{"kretschmann":{"opening":"The Kretschmann scalar $K$ of a massless scalar field falling in from infinity and making a black hole, against $x$ ($p = 2$), the same at every $\\theta$ and $\\phi$, beside the threshold $p = 1$.","clip":"We draw $K\\,\\ell^4e^{-4\\tau}$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-6}$ to $10^{4}$, the same in every view, and cut each curve where it leaves its panel: each $K$ passes below $10^{-6}$ within $x = 0.0003$ of the first ray, where it vanishes, and at $p = 2$ above $10^{4}$ beyond $x = 0.516$.","legend":[["line","K","$K$, the Kretschmann scalar"],["line","reference","the threshold, $p = 1$"]]},"ricci_scalar":{"opening":"The Ricci scalar $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ of a massless scalar field falling in from infinity and making a black hole, against $x$ ($p = 2$), the same at every $\\theta$ and $\\phi$, beside the threshold $p = 1$.","clip":"We draw $R^\\mu{}_\\mu\\,\\ell^2e^{-2\\tau}$ on a signed logarithmic scale, linear within $10^{-6}$ of zero, from $-10^{2}$ to $0$, the same in every view, and cut each curve where it leaves its panel, as $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ at $p = 2$ does beyond $x = 0.525$.","legend":[["line","R","$R^\\mu{}_\\mu$, the Ricci scalar"],["line","reference","the threshold, $p = 1$"]]}},"settings":"$p = 2$ and $\\tau = 0$, the light ray $u = -2\\ell$, with $\\ell$ any length, the unit of every length.","clip":"We draw $K\\,\\ell^4e^{-4\\tau}$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-6}$ to $10^{4}$ and $R^\\mu{}_\\mu\\,\\ell^2e^{-2\\tau}$ on a signed logarithmic scale, linear within $10^{-6}$ of zero, from $-10^{2}$ to $0$, the same in every view, and cut each curve where it leaves its panel: each $K$ passes below $10^{-6}$ within $x = 0.0003$ of the first ray, where it vanishes, and at $p = 2$ above $10^{4}$ beyond $x = 0.516$, and $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ at $p = 2$ below its scale beyond $x = 0.525$."}]}
